# Project root tombstone

When a project folder is moved or deleted in the file explorer, mark the old root in `deletedProjectRoots` **before any `await`**. In-flight autosaves and `ensureFolder` must not recreate empty `Library` / `System` / `Scenes` at the vacated path.

## Required

- On move: `deletedProjectRoots.add(oldRoot)` first, rebase in-memory paths, then `deletedProjectRoots.delete(newRoot)`.
- On delete: tombstone the whole project root, not just the manifest file.
- Create project-tree folders only through `ensureVaultFolder` in `utils/vaultFolders.ts` (or a wrapper that calls it). That helper refuses tombstoned paths.
- Do not call `vault.createFolder` on `Library`, `System`, `Scenes`, `Notes`, `Research`, or `Canvas` with a stale project path.

```typescript
// BAD — recreate empty folders at the old location
await this.app.vault.createFolder(`${oldProject}/Library`);

// GOOD — tombstone first, then only create under the live root
this.deletedProjectRoots.add(from);
await ensureVaultFolder(this.app, `${to}/Library`);
```

New folder-create helpers must honor `isDeletedProjectPath` / `isTombstonedProjectPath`. Do not remove the tombstone-before-await order in `handleProjectTreeFolderRename`.
